<article class="env-remark" id="0FA4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FA4">Remark <span data-tag="0FA4">42.38.11</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\mathcal{E}$ be a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. In general we write $X = \coprod X_ r$ as in Remark <a href="/tag/0ESW" data-tag="0ESW">42.38.10</a>. If only a finite number of the $X_ r$ are nonempty, then we can set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c_{top}(\mathcal{E}) = \sum \nolimits _ r c_ r(\mathcal{E}|_{X_ r}) \in A^*(X) = \bigoplus A^*(X_ r)  \]
</div>
  <p> where the equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/0FDZ" data-tag="0FDZ">42.35.4</a>. If infinitely many $X_ r$ are nonempty, we will use the same notation to denote </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c_{top}(\mathcal{E}) = \prod c_ r(\mathcal{E}|_{X_ r}) \in \prod A^ r(X_ r) \subset A^*(X)^\wedge  \]
</div>
  <p> see Remark <a href="/tag/0FE0" data-tag="0FE0">42.35.5</a> for notation. </p>
</article>